course: dictionary
lesson: 4778
title: Huff, puff and the sulky mood
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word huff can be a verb (you huff) or a noun (a huff). It can mean breathing out loudly, or a bad mood after you have been offended. Look at the words around it to find out which one it means. «Maya grumbled "it's only one dinner" and went to bed in a huff» tells you she was cross, not that she was out of breath.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If someone is breathing hard after running, huff means breathing out loudly. If someone has been upset and is sulking, huff means a bad mood. In the story «The Three Little Pigs», the wolf says «I'll huff and I'll puff and I'll blow your house down», and there huff means breathing hard.
explain: Look at the phrases too. «In a huff» and «go off in a huff» both mean sulking after you have been offended. «Huff and puff» can mean breathing hard, or complaining and making a fuss without doing much. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it right.
fact: Huff can be a verb: to breathe out loudly and heavily, often because you are tired or annoyed.
fact: Huff can be a noun: a bad mood, usually after being offended, as in «in a huff».
fact: «Huff and puff» can mean to breathe hard, or to complain and make a fuss without doing much.
fact: In «The Three Little Pigs», the wolf says «I'll huff and I'll puff», meaning he will breathe hard and blow hard.
fact: Maya went to bed in a huff, but in the morning she apologised, which shows a huff does not always last.
exercise: «Maya went to bed in a huff.» What does in a huff mean? | Happily ready for bed | Quickly and quietly | Very tired and out of breath | *In a bad mood after being offended
exercise: «I'll huff and I'll puff and I'll blow your house down», says the wolf. What does huff mean here? | To sing a happy song | To knock on the door politely | To cook a meal | *To breathe hard and loudly
exercise: Find and copy the word in «Maya grumbled "it's only one dinner" and went to bed in a huff» that shows she was complaining. | went | bed | *grumbled | dinner
test: Dad will huff and puff about the mess, but he always tidies it up in the end. What does huff and puff mean here? | Clean the whole house at once | Sing while he works | *Complain loudly and make a fuss | Run up the stairs fast
test: «Ella left the table in a huff.» How is Ella feeling? | Hungry | Sleepy | *Cross and sulking | Excited
exam: Which phrase means sulking after being offended? | breathe out | *in a huff | huff and puff | puff up
